    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d257-a1">

                <pb facs="0472" n="372" sameAs="frus:frus1884/pg372"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in 603.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Coates to Mr.
                            Davis.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1884-07-03"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 3,
                        1884</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: The case of Mr. Howard C. Walker is
                    simply that he is accused of an offense which was never proven; cast into jail
                    at Minatitlan, State of Vera Cruz, and refused bond or trial, and when our
                    consul went to see him was ordered away until they saw fit to let him in.</p>
                <p>Humbly, yours respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed>J. W. COATES, <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jr.</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Suwannee Station, Florida.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>P. S.—Many thanks for your kind reception and attention toward me this
                        morning.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
